messages:
Jules Park: quick flag from the console QA pass — compact action buttons on the Projects list are visually tight at 360px. The icon sits 4px from the label. Screenshot attached.
Marco Bianchi: yep saw it. We recently switched a few components to spacing.condensed (8px). Thats probably the culprit.
Priya Patel: proposal: keep spacing.condensed for layout grids but add component-specific tokens: --button-condensed-gap: 10px; --button-condensed-padding-x: 12px. This keeps global tokens stable.
Noah Rivera: agree on separate tokens. Dev note: prefer css variables so runtime theming/per-app overrides are easier. I'll add fallbacks to avoid regressions.
accessibility-bot: a11y reminder: icon+label buttons must maintain 44px hit target and expose aria-label when icon-only. Ensure :focus-visible styles are present.
Jules Park: also seeing toasts overlap the floating create button on mobile when an event triggers. The toast z-index is higher than the fab.
Marco Bianchi: ugh layering again. We have numeric z-values in a couple places. Can we switch to semantic layer tokens (layer.fab, layer.toast, layer.modal)? Then map to numbers per app.
Priya Patel: copy tweak: product prefers short CTAs on toasts like "Undo" / "Open". Also tooltips should show human copy not raw token names (no "spacing.condensed").
Noah Rivera: quick CSS experiment I'm pushing to a branch:
```
:root { --btn-condensed-gap: 10px; --btn-condensed-pad-y: 6px; --layer-toast: 1200; --layer-fab: 1150; }
.button--condensed { padding: var(--btn-condensed-pad-y) 12px; gap: var(--btn-condensed-gap); min-width: 44px; }
.toast { z-index: var(--layer-toast); right: 16px; bottom: 16px; }
.fab { z-index: var(--layer-fab); }
@media (max-width: 420px) { .toast-stack { display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:8px; } }
```
I'll add a small migration note for design tokens.
accessibility-bot: extra a11y checks: toasts should use aria-live="polite" for info and role="alert" for errors; if a toast contains an actionable control, ensure keyboard focus is supported and focus order is predictable.
Jules Park: great. Schedule a quick sync after standup to finalize token names and the PR copy. /remind me in 15
accessibility-bot: Reminder set for Jules Park in 15 minutes.
